  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">University of the South Pacific Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia has supported the University of the South Pacific (USP), which is a key source of graduates to industry and government in the region. USP provides the critical workforce for economic development, particularly in areas of new technology and responding to challenges such as climate change, natural disasters, renewable energy, and oceans, which are important to Australia&apos;s interests. The partnership provides flexible funding to support implementation of USP&apos;s Strategic Plan, including efforts to meet the tertiary education needs of the Pacific. The partnership also supports the Pacific to implement the Pacific Education Regional Framework (PacREF), with a focus on improving the quality of teacher education in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
